{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/674523-demons-and-virtue-vice","id":674523,"title":"Demons and Virtue & Vice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-22T13:14:14-07:00","id":674523,"title":"Demons and Virtue & Vice","content":"I'm not sure it ever occured to me before this morning, but upon reflection it's kind of weird to me that arguably the most inhuman splat in the nWoD works on Virtue &amp; Vice while other splats have their own unique splat-centric take on the idea. Is there a reasoning for that which I'm unaware of? How have angelic and demonic Virtue &amp; Vice played out at your table?<br /> <br /> (The most obvious answer is that they might not have come up with the idea of Virtue &amp; Vice alternatives while writing Demon, but I still think it's worth talking about.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T14:02:56-07:00","id":674572,"title":"","content":"I think the Virtue and Vice thing has been slanted by the fact that the first few monsters rolled out anew for second edition corebooks have been some of the more animalistic and slanted in nature. Virtue and Vice are still the baseline for mages, at the least. It does kind of stand out; it's been looking so far like basically everybody in the Dark Mother Club for Beasts has something else instead of Virtue and Vice, with the exceptions being &quot;still human even if supernaturally touched&quot; people like mages, psychics and hunters... and demons. The demons stick out.<br /> <br /> (My personal druthers would be to have more gribblies use Virtue and Vice, like maybe changelings or the Bound, and Deviants seem likely candidates. But I'm biased because, honestly, none of the alternative anchors have clicked for me. Virtue and Vice just feel like they cover all that ground already, but more intuitively.)<br /> <br /> My character in an ongoing game has a Virtue of <b>Clannish</b> and a Vice of <b>Cautious, </b>with a few opportunities for them to play out thus far. She's the most attached to her primary Cover out of the members of the ring, reluctant to let her work get in the way of her ability to live her everyday life with a family and friends, but her most daring and driven moments have been when her loyalties to close friends and family come out. She gets to know people, and when she does, she sticks by them; at one point she used Four Minutes Ago to rush <i>into</i> a confrontation with an ominous sorcerer she had been trying to avoid and bamboozle, because plan A using her friends as field agents went poorly. (She's also easily the least combat-capable of the ring.) Her bad habits tend to come out when she plays it too safe; she's also used Four Minutes Ago to ditch her ringmates when they accompanied her on a research trip into the city and a crazy/misguided zombie lady trapped her with some graffiti. And even in the case above, plan B, direct confrontation, threats and bluffing with the sorcerer, turned out to be far more effective than plan A.<br /> <br /> Another character in the same game has the Virtue of <b>Outrage.</b> Her moves toward human psychology and empathy have been motivated by trying to mend perceived injustices, after having been employed as one of God's erasers. She doesn't make friends with peers much (and doesn't really view humans as peers in the first place), but she does bond with victims and charges to protect, and her greatest risks are taken when she gets personally invested in a travesty of justice. It first came out visibly when she inadvertantly gave a cornered and manifested enemy angel time to escape, because rather than just try to hack him apart, she vented her anger at her own Fall by taunting him in an attempt to provoke him into Falling as well, as a sort of misplaced poetic justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T14:37:30-07:00","id":674593,"title":"","content":"Worth remembering: Demons are encouraged to have very strange and contradictory Virtues and Vices.<br /> <br /> But at the end of the day, this is still a game about divine and fallen beings. Concepts of Good and Evil are subtly poles that Angels and Demons wildlly spin around in the orbit of, switching from one gravity to the other as they navigate a disturbingly grey space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T14:41:59-07:00","id":674595,"title":"","content":"I think it fits for creatures called Demons to have Virtues and Vices, if for no other reason than to fit the genre. It also makes sense for them to have a similar baseline to mortals, since their whole ethos is to pretend to be human. Another way to think of it is that Mask/Dirge, Blood/Bone, Life/Legend are a bit more external, whereas Vice/Virtue are more internal, and a Demon doesn't necessarily have to alter her Cover's behaviour to compensate.<br /> <br /> This is all after the fact, of course. It might just be that it was set before the alternate splat Anchors (I <i>think </i>that's the general term for them now) were chosen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T15:20:38-07:00","id":674611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/674523-demons-and-virtue-vice#post674523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure it ever occured to me before this morning, but upon reflection it's kind of weird to me that arguably the most inhuman splat in the nWoD works on Virtue &amp; Vice while other splats have their own unique splat-centric take on the idea. Is there a reasoning for that which I'm unaware of? How have angelic and demonic Virtue &amp; Vice played out at your table?<br /> <br /> (The most obvious answer is that they might not have come up with the idea of Virtue &amp; Vice alternatives while writing Demon, but I still think it's worth talking about.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Biologically most inhuman.<br /> <br /> The nature of a Fall is to become far, far more spiritually human, and each angel has the potential for that. All it takes is one ignored order...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T04:54:21-07:00","id":675116,"title":"","content":"I actually like that they possess Virtue and Vice but can have selections in either category that are very strange. For me it helps to pin them down as alien much better than any of the monsters, whose various systems seem to be more about retaining their humanity. Demons are never human, they don't think like a human, and in my Demon games Virtue and Vice have proven a really good way to play that up. Even though Angels and Demons are very good at disguising themselves as mortals, in the end, there is always something off about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T10:27:25-07:00","id":675375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/674523-demons-and-virtue-vice#post674523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure it ever occured to me before this morning, but upon reflection it's kind of weird to me that arguably the most inhuman splat in the nWoD works on Virtue &amp; Vice while other splats have their own unique splat-centric take on the idea. Is there a reasoning for that which I'm unaware of? How have angelic and demonic Virtue &amp; Vice played out at your table?<br /> <br /> (The most obvious answer is that they might not have come up with the idea of Virtue &amp; Vice alternatives while writing Demon, but I still think it's worth talking about.)</div> </div> </div> </div> One, despite being called Virtue and Vice, they're actually not really either. First of all, the example list is different than the one for mortals. Mechanically, gaining willpower works the same, but the actual categories are different. And you're encouraged to come up with your own categories as well.<br /> <br /> Two, there's no separate Virtue list and separate Vice list. Murderous is a vice for every last mortal human on the planet. For a demon, it can be a Virtue, a Vice, neither, or both. You can have Charity as a Vice, a guilty weakness. You can double down on &quot;bad&quot; or &quot;good&quot; traits, be an inverse with a bad Virtue and good Vice.<br /> <br /> Its thematically appropriate for the Unchained to be tied to something resembling human morality, but twisted. Super embodiemnt of sins, or even embodiment of virtues for a fallen angel looking for repentence. Or something that encourages detachment from humanity all together.<br /> <br /> DtD's Virtue and Vice are really very flexible. Don't be fooled by the name - you can do pretty much anything you want with it in ways humans can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}